{"repositoryId":404774744,"availability":"available","full":"hugovalepereira/vitral-image-format","name":"vitral-image-format","description":"Vitral: Blend modes that survive export. A proposal for an image format that keeps multiply, screen and their relatives inside a valid PNG. Spec, Rust reference implementation, CLI and web polyfill.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2021-09-09T15:28:05Z","updated":"2026-10-16T19:30:45Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hugovalepereira.github.io/vitral-image-format/","topics":["blend-modes","compositing","figma","figma-plugin","graphics","image-format","mix-blend-mode","png","rust","webassembly"],"demo":"https://hugovalepereira.github.io/vitral-image-format/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:12:48.846Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T07:12:48.846Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T07:12:48.846Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T07:12:48.846Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Vitral is a proposal for an image format that carries its own blend modes. What multiplies in Figma, Illustrator or Photoshop keeps multiplying on the website, without anyone rebuilding it: multiply, screen and their relatives, mixed freely per pixel in one PNG.","PNG has transparency. Vitral has light and filter.","It is also a valid PNG. Where nothing is behind it, and in software that has never heard of Vitral, it shows each pixel's own colour: the same image a normal PNG export would give you. It is never worse than the PNG you would export today."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hugovalepereira/vitral-image-format/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9ab8820c57941031c252bb4a2f6398507f87c7873973b2a64a596b71ac5f4773","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T07:12:48.957Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:12:48.957Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Vitral is a proposal for an image